WEBVTT

00:00:01.335 --> 00:00:03.128
<i>(IF I HAD A HEART</i> PLAYING)

00:00:52.678 --> 00:00:55.055
Tell me what

00:00:52.678 --> 00:00:55.055
it is you want.

00:00:56.015 --> 00:00:58.726
Are you unhappy?

00:00:58.768 --> 00:01:00.519
Do you think the gods

00:00:58.768 --> 00:01:00.519
have cheated you?

00:01:08.987 --> 00:01:11.990
I want my old

00:01:08.987 --> 00:01:11.990
position back.

00:01:12.031 --> 00:01:14.074
I was never meant

00:01:12.031 --> 00:01:14.074
to be a servant,

00:01:15.367 --> 00:01:17.077
a slave, a friend.

00:01:19.831 --> 00:01:22.583
I am bitter

00:01:19.831 --> 00:01:22.583
and I am angry.

00:01:22.625 --> 00:01:25.544
Everything I had,

00:01:22.625 --> 00:01:25.544
everything I possessed,

00:01:25.586 --> 00:01:27.964
everything that

00:01:25.586 --> 00:01:27.964
I was,

00:01:28.006 --> 00:01:29.841
has been stripped

00:01:28.006 --> 00:01:29.841
away from me.

00:01:34.136 --> 00:01:36.138
And my anger is

00:01:34.136 --> 00:01:36.138
like a stone...

00:01:41.226 --> 00:01:43.771
A stone that I carry

00:01:41.226 --> 00:01:43.771
inside me that...

00:01:45.606 --> 00:01:47.107
Weighs me down.

00:01:49.527 --> 00:01:51.111
I cannot lift it.

00:01:51.153 --> 00:01:53.322
In some ways,

00:01:51.153 --> 00:01:53.322
you are still fortunate.

00:01:54.782 --> 00:01:56.408
Ragnar could

00:01:54.782 --> 00:01:56.408
have had you killed,

00:01:56.450 --> 00:01:58.410
at the same time

00:01:56.450 --> 00:01:58.410
as your husband.

00:01:58.452 --> 00:02:02.874
I am supposed to be

00:01:58.452 --> 00:02:02.874
eternally grateful,

00:01:58.452 --> 00:02:02.874
to my husband's killer?

00:02:02.915 --> 00:02:06.044
I ask you once more,

00:02:02.915 --> 00:02:06.044
why you have come here,

00:02:06.085 --> 00:02:08.504
if you do not think, I can

00:02:06.085 --> 00:02:08.504
offer you any comfort.

00:02:10.255 --> 00:02:11.757
I want to know,

00:02:15.302 --> 00:02:18.597
will the gods ever

00:02:15.302 --> 00:02:18.597
smile on me again?

00:02:20.265 --> 00:02:23.394
The gods will always

00:02:20.265 --> 00:02:23.394
smile on brave women,

00:02:24.186 --> 00:02:26.856
like the Valkyries,

00:02:26.898 --> 00:02:31.151
those furies who

00:02:26.898 --> 00:02:31.151
men fear and desire.

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:19.992
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

00:03:24.455 --> 00:03:27.499
You'll have to forgive

00:03:24.455 --> 00:03:27.499
the poverty of the feast.

00:03:27.541 --> 00:03:29.334
It has been a hard winter.

00:03:31.253 --> 00:03:33.047
We had to burn

00:03:31.253 --> 00:03:33.047
our own grain stores,

00:03:33.089 --> 00:03:34.882
to rid ourselves

00:03:33.089 --> 00:03:34.882
of Jarl Borg.

00:03:34.924 --> 00:03:36.592
So I heard.

00:03:39.219 --> 00:03:41.055
Tell us, Erlendur,

00:03:41.097 --> 00:03:43.390
what happened in

00:03:41.097 --> 00:03:43.390
England after we left?

00:03:47.352 --> 00:03:49.063
We were betrayed

00:03:47.352 --> 00:03:49.063
by King Ecbert.

00:03:49.688 --> 00:03:51.732
We made contact, and

00:03:51.774 --> 00:03:56.528
your Christian friend

00:03:51.774 --> 00:03:56.528
Athelstan, arranged for

00:03:51.774 --> 00:03:56.528
further talks, or so he said.

00:03:56.570 --> 00:03:58.906
In retrospect, I wonder

00:03:56.570 --> 00:03:58.906
who's side he was really on.

00:04:00.616 --> 00:04:02.242
In any case,

00:04:00.616 --> 00:04:02.242
the trickster was at work.

00:04:03.661 --> 00:04:07.123
Ecbert never meant to

00:04:03.661 --> 00:04:07.123
honor his promises to you.

00:04:07.165 --> 00:04:09.625
We were betrayed,

00:04:07.165 --> 00:04:09.625
taken by surprise.

00:04:09.667 --> 00:04:11.710
There was

00:04:09.667 --> 00:04:11.710
a great slaughter.

00:04:11.752 --> 00:04:14.213
Erlendur and I barely

00:04:11.752 --> 00:04:14.213
escaped with our lives.

00:04:14.254 --> 00:04:15.798
What about Athelstan?

00:04:17.008 --> 00:04:18.801
Where is he now?

00:04:18.843 --> 00:04:20.678
If he is fortunate,

00:04:18.843 --> 00:04:20.678
he died in battle.

00:04:22.180 --> 00:04:24.264
In any case,

00:04:22.180 --> 00:04:24.264
let's not speak of him.

00:04:25.307 --> 00:04:27.392
He was a

00:04:25.307 --> 00:04:27.392
worthless individual.

00:04:29.895 --> 00:04:32.731
Poor Athelstan.

00:04:32.773 --> 00:04:35.484
My sister and I grew

00:04:32.773 --> 00:04:35.484
to love him, when

00:04:32.773 --> 00:04:35.484
we were children.

00:04:35.526 --> 00:04:37.611
FLOKI: He fooled you,

00:04:35.526 --> 00:04:37.611
young Bjorn.

00:04:39.030 --> 00:04:41.032
He never denounced his

00:04:39.030 --> 00:04:41.032
Christian God.

00:04:41.991 --> 00:04:43.575
He was our enemy.

00:04:45.327 --> 00:04:48.164
We should rejoice

00:04:45.327 --> 00:04:48.164
at his death.

00:04:49.665 --> 00:04:50.833
So...

00:04:52.960 --> 00:04:55.129
What do you intend

00:04:52.960 --> 00:04:55.129
on doing now?

00:04:55.171 --> 00:04:58.298
What do you think, Ragnar?

00:04:58.340 --> 00:05:01.927
I intend on gaining

00:04:58.340 --> 00:05:01.927
revenge on King Ecbert.

00:05:01.969 --> 00:05:03.637
We should plan a raid

00:05:01.969 --> 00:05:03.637
as soon as possible.

00:05:05.014 --> 00:05:07.391
ROLLO: I would be very

00:05:05.014 --> 00:05:07.391
happy to take part in it.

00:05:07.432 --> 00:05:09.309
King Ecbert should

00:05:07.432 --> 00:05:09.309
certainly be punished.

00:05:11.687 --> 00:05:13.105
I agree.

00:05:14.148 --> 00:05:15.315
We should return

00:05:14.148 --> 00:05:15.315
to Wessex.

00:05:17.442 --> 00:05:20.029
But first,

00:05:17.442 --> 00:05:20.029
Jarl Borg must

00:05:17.442 --> 00:05:20.029
pay the price,

00:05:20.071 --> 00:05:21.989
for what he did

00:05:20.071 --> 00:05:21.989
to my family,

00:05:22.865 --> 00:05:24.200
and to our people.

00:05:26.660 --> 00:05:27.578
(GASPS)

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:30.998
Forgive me, master.

00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:32.457
No, it doesn't matter.

00:05:34.418 --> 00:05:35.920
HORIK: I understand,

00:05:34.418 --> 00:05:35.920
completely,

00:05:35.961 --> 00:05:38.256
and if I were you,

00:05:35.961 --> 00:05:38.256
I would feel the same way.

00:05:38.297 --> 00:05:40.340
But we must

00:05:38.297 --> 00:05:40.340
remember our agreement

00:05:40.382 --> 00:05:42.676
and what it was for.

00:05:42.718 --> 00:05:47.223
We would sail west to

00:05:42.718 --> 00:05:47.223
raid and to colonize.

00:05:47.265 --> 00:05:48.766
That was your dream, Ragnar,

00:05:50.101 --> 00:05:52.853
and I have come

00:05:50.101 --> 00:05:52.853
to share it.

00:05:52.895 --> 00:05:56.607
But now, we have neither

00:05:52.895 --> 00:05:56.607
the men nor the ships,

00:05:56.648 --> 00:05:58.483
to realize our dreams.

00:06:00.278 --> 00:06:01.612
What are you saying?

00:06:01.653 --> 00:06:04.364
I think we should

00:06:01.653 --> 00:06:04.364
go back to Jarl Borg.

00:06:04.406 --> 00:06:08.119
He is licking his wounds.

00:06:04.406 --> 00:06:08.119
He is no longer as

00:06:04.406 --> 00:06:08.119
strong as he was.

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:11.330
And, yet, we need him.

00:06:11.371 --> 00:06:13.791
We cannot go west

00:06:11.371 --> 00:06:13.791
without his ships.

00:06:14.792 --> 00:06:16.418
And so, once again,

00:06:16.460 --> 00:06:19.213
we should ask him

00:06:16.460 --> 00:06:19.213
to join our alliance.

00:06:24.676 --> 00:06:26.470
Don't listen to him.

00:06:28.722 --> 00:06:31.267
But who should

00:06:28.722 --> 00:06:31.267
go to Jarl Borg?

00:06:31.309 --> 00:06:34.436
I think it should

00:06:31.309 --> 00:06:34.436
be you, Rollo.

00:06:34.478 --> 00:06:37.815
After all, you know

00:06:34.478 --> 00:06:37.815
him better than anyone.

00:06:39.942 --> 00:06:41.110
What do you think?

00:06:49.910 --> 00:06:51.787
Farewell, my love.

00:06:51.829 --> 00:06:54.748
I will pray to Thor

00:06:51.829 --> 00:06:54.748
that he grant

00:06:51.829 --> 00:06:54.748
you safe passage.

00:06:54.790 --> 00:06:55.833
MAN: Throw that.

00:06:58.794 --> 00:07:02.464
May you have success, Rollo,

00:06:58.794 --> 00:07:02.464
for the sake of all of us.

00:07:02.506 --> 00:07:04.008
MAN: Man your stations.

00:07:04.049 --> 00:07:05.384
MAN 2: Stores aboard.

00:07:14.393 --> 00:07:16.395
MAN 3: All the men aboard!

00:07:16.436 --> 00:07:17.521
Rollo.

00:07:18.814 --> 00:07:20.358
MAN: Try the sail then.

00:07:20.399 --> 00:07:21.441
I, too, wish you well.

00:07:23.485 --> 00:07:25.821
Those words mean

00:07:23.485 --> 00:07:25.821
a lot coming from you.

00:07:25.863 --> 00:07:26.822
They were hard to say.

00:07:28.032 --> 00:07:29.449
Now they are said.

00:07:35.873 --> 00:07:37.249
Cast away!

00:07:37.291 --> 00:07:38.500
MAN: Ready the oars!

00:08:06.862 --> 00:08:08.947
It has an unusual

00:08:06.862 --> 00:08:08.947
taste, wine.

00:08:10.657 --> 00:08:13.285
But then, you're

00:08:10.657 --> 00:08:13.285
an unusual woman, Siggy.

00:08:17.039 --> 00:08:18.999
You don't like wine?

00:08:17.039 --> 00:08:18.999
(SPITS)

00:08:19.041 --> 00:08:20.418
It's horrible.

00:08:20.459 --> 00:08:23.795
The finer things in life

00:08:20.459 --> 00:08:23.795
are an acquired taste.

00:08:23.837 --> 00:08:27.466
I hope you do not

00:08:23.837 --> 00:08:27.466
mind I brought my

00:08:23.837 --> 00:08:27.466
son with me?

00:08:27.507 --> 00:08:30.510
I want him to start to

00:08:27.507 --> 00:08:30.510
understand the game.

00:08:31.845 --> 00:08:33.138
The game?

00:08:33.180 --> 00:08:34.514
The game you and I play.

00:08:36.392 --> 00:08:38.936
The game Ragnar

00:08:36.392 --> 00:08:38.936
tries to play.

00:08:41.230 --> 00:08:43.065
Are you sure

00:08:41.230 --> 00:08:43.065
it is a game?

00:08:46.151 --> 00:08:48.320
Why do you invite

00:08:46.151 --> 00:08:48.320
me to your bed?

00:08:50.406 --> 00:08:52.657
Why do you tell me

00:08:50.406 --> 00:08:52.657
things about Ragnar?

00:08:58.080 --> 00:09:01.541
Everything I do,

00:08:58.080 --> 00:09:01.541
I do for Rollo.

00:09:04.878 --> 00:09:06.505
And not for yourself?

00:09:07.298 --> 00:09:09.258
If Rollo rises,

00:09:07.298 --> 00:09:09.258
I rise also.

00:09:11.469 --> 00:09:13.137
And you need my help.

00:09:13.178 --> 00:09:15.055
(CHUCKLING)

00:09:15.097 --> 00:09:16.890
Well, what do you think,

00:09:17.682 --> 00:09:18.892
King Horik?

00:09:20.311 --> 00:09:22.062
And what would you do,

00:09:20.311 --> 00:09:22.062
Siggy,

00:09:23.481 --> 00:09:25.565
for my continued

00:09:23.481 --> 00:09:25.565
and active support?

00:09:28.944 --> 00:09:30.237
(LAUGHING)

00:09:30.279 --> 00:09:32.697
My son is ignorant

00:09:30.279 --> 00:09:32.697
of the game,

00:09:32.739 --> 00:09:35.700
and strangely ignorant

00:09:32.739 --> 00:09:35.700
of other things as well.

00:09:35.742 --> 00:09:37.035
(CHUCKLES)

00:09:37.077 --> 00:09:39.997
He's only been

00:09:37.077 --> 00:09:39.997
with a few women,

00:09:37.077 --> 00:09:39.997
and they were nothing...

00:09:40.038 --> 00:09:41.706
Slaves, girls.

00:09:45.127 --> 00:09:47.463
I want him to

00:09:45.127 --> 00:09:47.463
enjoy the attentions

00:09:48.547 --> 00:09:51.842
of an experienced,

00:09:48.547 --> 00:09:51.842
free woman.

00:09:52.592 --> 00:09:53.593
(EXHALING)

00:10:29.254 --> 00:10:31.715
Erlendur, come.

00:11:23.350 --> 00:11:26.520
SIGVARD: <i> She sees a hall</i>

00:11:23.350 --> 00:11:26.520
<i>more fair than the sun,</i>

00:11:26.562 --> 00:11:29.356
<i>thatched with gold, at Gimle.</i>

00:11:29.398 --> 00:11:33.444
<i>There shall the gods</i>

00:11:29.398 --> 00:11:33.444
<i>in innocence dwell,</i>

00:11:33.485 --> 00:11:36.154
and live forever

00:11:33.485 --> 00:11:36.154
a life of bliss.

00:11:36.196 --> 00:11:37.239
(BURPING)

00:11:38.782 --> 00:11:40.951
Why don't we have poets

00:11:38.782 --> 00:11:40.951
here anymore?

00:11:42.911 --> 00:11:44.704
Poets to entertain us.

00:11:45.247 --> 00:11:46.706
Sing to us.

00:11:47.165 --> 00:11:50.252
Make us laugh.

00:11:50.294 --> 00:11:54.172
I remember when

00:11:50.294 --> 00:11:54.172
this great hall,

00:11:50.294 --> 00:11:54.172
was always full of laughter.

00:11:56.091 --> 00:11:58.718
Laughter and good

00:11:56.091 --> 00:11:58.718
fellowship.

00:12:00.971 --> 00:12:02.431
WOMAN: You can see

00:12:00.971 --> 00:12:02.431
it in her eyes.

00:12:02.473 --> 00:12:04.933
My wife has

00:12:02.473 --> 00:12:04.933
returned to me.

00:12:06.143 --> 00:12:07.227
(CHUCKLING)

00:12:07.269 --> 00:12:09.271
That's good.

00:12:09.313 --> 00:12:10.897
(SCATTERED LAUGHTER)

00:12:10.939 --> 00:12:14.276
She went without

00:12:10.939 --> 00:12:14.276
my permission.

00:12:14.318 --> 00:12:18.280
But, as you can all see,

00:12:14.318 --> 00:12:18.280
she has come back,

00:12:14.318 --> 00:12:18.280
and I love her for it.

00:12:19.698 --> 00:12:24.286
After all, what man

00:12:19.698 --> 00:12:24.286
wouldn't be pleased,

00:12:25.621 --> 00:12:27.747
at the return

00:12:25.621 --> 00:12:27.747
of such a wife?

00:12:31.502 --> 00:12:32.836
<i>Skal.</i>

00:12:32.877 --> 00:12:34.296
ALL: <i> Skal!</i>

00:12:37.215 --> 00:12:39.468
<i>Skal,</i> husband.

00:12:48.935 --> 00:12:50.354
Unfortunately,

00:12:51.689 --> 00:12:53.773
you left my

00:12:51.689 --> 00:12:53.773
stepson behind.

00:12:56.443 --> 00:12:57.777
MAN: It's time to leave.

00:13:02.366 --> 00:13:03.783
Gerta, take my hand.

00:13:02.366 --> 00:13:03.783
Come. Come.

00:13:05.744 --> 00:13:07.787
He wanted to stay

00:13:05.744 --> 00:13:07.787
with his father.

00:13:09.498 --> 00:13:10.832
He's old enough to decide.

00:13:10.874 --> 00:13:12.917
Is it not enough

00:13:10.874 --> 00:13:12.917
that I came back?

00:13:12.959 --> 00:13:17.047
No, it's not enough,

00:13:12.959 --> 00:13:17.047
my dear wife,

00:13:17.088 --> 00:13:19.132
it's... It's not enough.

00:13:19.174 --> 00:13:21.968
Of course it's not enough.

00:13:19.174 --> 00:13:21.968
It's an insult to me.

00:13:22.010 --> 00:13:24.638
What else could

00:13:22.010 --> 00:13:24.638
I have done?

00:13:24.680 --> 00:13:26.598
His father is

00:13:24.680 --> 00:13:26.598
Ragnar Lothbrok.

00:13:27.349 --> 00:13:28.600
(METAL CLATTERING)

00:13:32.187 --> 00:13:33.397
Who is this

00:13:34.314 --> 00:13:36.775
Ragnar Lothbrok?

00:13:36.816 --> 00:13:39.861
Nothing but a windbag,

00:13:36.816 --> 00:13:39.861
an opportunist.

00:13:39.903 --> 00:13:42.239
A man so bloated

00:13:39.903 --> 00:13:42.239
with self-importance,

00:13:42.280 --> 00:13:45.242
he pretends to be

00:13:42.280 --> 00:13:45.242
descended from Odin!

00:13:45.283 --> 00:13:46.451
(ALL LAUGHING)

00:13:48.203 --> 00:13:49.829
He doesn't need to

00:13:48.203 --> 00:13:49.829
pretend anything.

00:13:57.421 --> 00:14:00.591
Now I know for sure why

00:13:57.421 --> 00:14:00.591
you went to defend him.

00:14:02.217 --> 00:14:05.845
Not to repulse

00:14:02.217 --> 00:14:05.845
a foreign invader,

00:14:02.217 --> 00:14:05.845
as you lied to me,

00:14:07.305 --> 00:14:09.849
but because

00:14:07.305 --> 00:14:09.849
you're still in

00:14:07.305 --> 00:14:09.849
love with him.

00:14:11.976 --> 00:14:15.855
You're still in love

00:14:11.976 --> 00:14:15.855
with Ragnar Lothbrok,

00:14:18.400 --> 00:14:21.278
aren't you, wife?

00:14:28.702 --> 00:14:31.663
You can sleep

00:14:28.702 --> 00:14:31.663
alone tonight.

00:14:31.705 --> 00:14:34.207
I have made

00:14:31.705 --> 00:14:34.207
other arrangements.

00:14:39.296 --> 00:14:40.505
(DOOR CREAKING)

00:14:47.846 --> 00:14:48.972
(TREMBLING BREATH)

00:14:49.431 --> 00:14:50.724
(FOOTSTEPS)

00:15:00.900 --> 00:15:01.901
(ALL GRUNTING)

00:15:26.259 --> 00:15:29.596
Master, can I help you?

00:15:29.638 --> 00:15:32.808
I was going to ask

00:15:29.638 --> 00:15:32.808
you the same question.

00:15:32.850 --> 00:15:34.184
Those buckets

00:15:32.850 --> 00:15:34.184
look very heavy.

00:15:34.893 --> 00:15:36.436
I'm used to it.

00:15:41.316 --> 00:15:42.192
What is your name?

00:15:43.527 --> 00:15:44.736
Porunn.

00:15:47.739 --> 00:15:48.990
Sit a moment.

00:15:50.033 --> 00:15:51.535
I have to finish my work.

00:15:51.576 --> 00:15:53.036
It is all right.

00:16:11.262 --> 00:16:12.931
Where do you sleep?

00:16:13.431 --> 00:16:15.392
In that barn

00:16:15.433 --> 00:16:17.895
with the other

00:16:15.433 --> 00:16:17.895
servants and animals.

00:16:19.312 --> 00:16:20.564
Do you...

00:16:21.732 --> 00:16:23.191
Have a boyfriend?

00:16:27.028 --> 00:16:28.405
Of course!

00:16:33.326 --> 00:16:35.119
I must finish my work.

00:16:48.049 --> 00:16:50.134
ASLAUG: She is

00:16:48.049 --> 00:16:50.134
remarkably good looking.

00:16:54.472 --> 00:16:56.099
If you say so.

00:17:03.273 --> 00:17:05.817
Why do you let Horik

00:17:03.273 --> 00:17:05.817
decide everything?

00:17:09.613 --> 00:17:11.865
Can you really

00:17:09.613 --> 00:17:11.865
forgive Jarl Borg?

00:17:14.868 --> 00:17:17.913
Do you know how much I

00:17:14.868 --> 00:17:17.913
suffered because of him?

00:17:17.955 --> 00:17:19.998
How much your

00:17:17.955 --> 00:17:19.998
son suffered?

00:17:22.292 --> 00:17:23.334
Yes.

00:17:24.669 --> 00:17:26.254
I know.

00:17:26.296 --> 00:17:28.381
But you do

00:17:26.296 --> 00:17:28.381
nothing about it!

00:17:29.466 --> 00:17:31.134
By insulting and

00:17:29.466 --> 00:17:31.134
humiliating me,

00:17:31.175 --> 00:17:34.053
he insulted and

00:17:31.175 --> 00:17:34.053
humiliated you.

00:17:36.306 --> 00:17:38.642
My father never would

00:17:36.306 --> 00:17:38.642
have allowed such a thing.

00:17:38.683 --> 00:17:40.811
He would have

00:17:38.683 --> 00:17:40.811
been revenged.

00:17:43.814 --> 00:17:46.065
Your father cannot

00:17:43.814 --> 00:17:46.065
do too much now,

00:17:47.191 --> 00:17:48.693
being dead.

00:18:15.261 --> 00:18:16.638
What is wrong?

00:18:18.723 --> 00:18:20.099
You are quite safe.

00:18:24.145 --> 00:18:25.438
Where is he?

00:18:48.795 --> 00:18:50.254
Sit down.

00:19:05.395 --> 00:19:06.354
What is that?

00:19:11.442 --> 00:19:13.319
The skull of my first wife.

00:19:15.196 --> 00:19:17.156
She continues to advise me.

00:19:21.786 --> 00:19:23.162
Is that fair to her?

00:19:25.749 --> 00:19:26.875
So...

00:19:28.585 --> 00:19:31.088
Your brother

00:19:28.585 --> 00:19:31.088
wants me to come

00:19:28.585 --> 00:19:31.088
and fight for him?

00:19:32.338 --> 00:19:35.341
He wants to rebuild

00:19:32.338 --> 00:19:35.341
the original alliance

00:19:35.383 --> 00:19:37.176
between himself,

00:19:35.383 --> 00:19:37.176
King Horik, and you.

00:19:39.888 --> 00:19:44.183
He believes that,

00:19:39.888 --> 00:19:44.183
in our small countries,

00:19:45.476 --> 00:19:47.979
cooperation is

00:19:45.476 --> 00:19:47.979
the only way forward.

00:19:49.898 --> 00:19:52.191
So, he does not

00:19:49.898 --> 00:19:52.191
want revenge upon me?

00:19:53.610 --> 00:19:57.238
After all,

00:19:53.610 --> 00:19:57.238
I invaded his lands.

00:19:57.280 --> 00:20:00.033
Men like you

00:19:57.280 --> 00:20:00.033
and I will always

00:19:57.280 --> 00:20:00.033
look for revenge.

00:20:02.577 --> 00:20:04.370
Ragnar looks beyond.

00:20:04.412 --> 00:20:07.373
Then he is a most

00:20:04.412 --> 00:20:07.373
extraordinary man indeed.

00:20:09.042 --> 00:20:11.252
As forgiving

00:20:09.042 --> 00:20:11.252
as a Christian!

00:20:13.088 --> 00:20:15.214
He is also

00:20:13.088 --> 00:20:15.214
a practical man.

00:20:17.175 --> 00:20:19.761
He and King Horik

00:20:17.175 --> 00:20:19.761
have lost a lot of men.

00:20:20.845 --> 00:20:23.222
They need you to

00:20:20.845 --> 00:20:23.222
help them raid.

00:20:30.521 --> 00:20:32.356
BORG: What do

00:20:30.521 --> 00:20:32.356
you say, my love?

00:20:39.530 --> 00:20:40.740
(SNIFFING)

00:20:44.869 --> 00:20:46.579
You think I should go?

00:20:52.961 --> 00:20:54.754
She thinks I should go.

00:20:56.673 --> 00:20:58.716
Torvi, bring some mead.

00:20:58.758 --> 00:21:00.885
Yes, Jarl Borg.

00:21:00.927 --> 00:21:04.222
You and I must drink, to this

00:21:00.927 --> 00:21:04.222
most unexpected,

00:21:04.931 --> 00:21:07.100
but not unwelcome event.

00:21:07.142 --> 00:21:08.559
My wife will join us.

00:21:11.771 --> 00:21:13.231
Pour it in here.

00:21:21.031 --> 00:21:22.115
<i>Skal.</i>

00:21:27.620 --> 00:21:28.746
<i>Skal.</i>

00:22:08.953 --> 00:22:11.248
You have a great

00:22:08.953 --> 00:22:11.248
gift, Athelstan.

00:22:11.289 --> 00:22:14.751
I believe it is a...

00:22:11.289 --> 00:22:14.751
A divine gift.

00:22:16.586 --> 00:22:18.629
Thank you, sire.

00:22:18.671 --> 00:22:21.091
I thought I might

00:22:18.671 --> 00:22:21.091
have forgotten, but...

00:22:22.967 --> 00:22:25.303
I love these materials.

00:22:25.344 --> 00:22:29.224
Brushes, the paints,

00:22:25.344 --> 00:22:29.224
the colors.

00:22:31.059 --> 00:22:33.978
I had not appreciated

00:22:31.059 --> 00:22:33.978
how much I missed my work.

00:22:34.020 --> 00:22:37.148
The pagans have

00:22:34.020 --> 00:22:37.148
nothing like it?

00:22:37.190 --> 00:22:38.233
No.

00:22:38.900 --> 00:22:40.443
They have no art.

00:22:41.694 --> 00:22:43.404
They can neither

00:22:41.694 --> 00:22:43.404
read nor write,

00:22:43.446 --> 00:22:45.823
except for their

00:22:43.446 --> 00:22:45.823
carved runes.

00:22:45.865 --> 00:22:46.866
Hmm.

00:22:48.868 --> 00:22:51.288
And their gods?

00:22:51.329 --> 00:22:56.251
Uh, Odin and Thor

00:22:51.329 --> 00:22:56.251
and Freyr.

00:22:51.329 --> 00:22:56.251
(CHUCKLING)

00:22:56.293 --> 00:22:58.461
How strange you

00:22:56.293 --> 00:22:58.461
must have found them.

00:23:01.047 --> 00:23:02.673
In some ways, yes.

00:23:03.883 --> 00:23:05.384
In other ways...

00:23:06.427 --> 00:23:07.804
In other ways?

00:23:11.224 --> 00:23:14.060
Their gods are very old.

00:23:14.102 --> 00:23:17.147
And sometimes I could

00:23:14.102 --> 00:23:17.147
not help noticing,

00:23:14.102 --> 00:23:17.147
some similarities

00:23:17.188 --> 00:23:19.190
with our own God,

00:23:17.188 --> 00:23:19.190
and his son.

00:23:21.109 --> 00:23:22.986
For example,

00:23:21.109 --> 00:23:22.986
their god, Odin,

00:23:23.027 --> 00:23:26.489
whom they call the All-father,

00:23:23.027 --> 00:23:26.489
the god of gods,

00:23:26.530 --> 00:23:29.659
wanted to discover

00:23:26.530 --> 00:23:29.659
what it was like to die.

00:23:29.700 --> 00:23:32.329
So, according to their

00:23:29.700 --> 00:23:32.329
stories and traditions,

00:23:32.370 --> 00:23:34.289
Odin hung himself

00:23:32.370 --> 00:23:34.289
from a tree,

00:23:35.915 --> 00:23:39.336
and a pagan servant,

00:23:35.915 --> 00:23:39.336
stabbed him in his side

00:23:35.915 --> 00:23:39.336
with a spear,

00:23:39.377 --> 00:23:41.338
just like the Romans

00:23:39.377 --> 00:23:41.338
did to Christ.

00:23:46.717 --> 00:23:48.011
Come with me.

00:23:53.683 --> 00:23:55.226
Tell me honestly.

00:23:56.394 --> 00:23:58.562
What do you

00:23:56.394 --> 00:23:58.562
think of these works?

00:24:02.483 --> 00:24:05.195
I find them

00:24:02.483 --> 00:24:05.195
indescribably

00:24:02.483 --> 00:24:05.195
beautiful.

00:24:05.236 --> 00:24:06.988
But they are

00:24:05.236 --> 00:24:06.988
clearly pagan.

00:24:09.366 --> 00:24:10.367
(CHUCKLING)

00:24:12.618 --> 00:24:15.705
You are only a monk,

00:24:12.618 --> 00:24:15.705
Athelstan, and yet,

00:24:12.618 --> 00:24:15.705
somehow, I...

00:24:16.873 --> 00:24:19.292
I begin to trust you.

00:24:16.873 --> 00:24:19.292
I feel you...

00:24:21.169 --> 00:24:23.004
You are a kindred spirit.

00:24:27.758 --> 00:24:28.843
Who?

00:24:30.345 --> 00:24:32.889
Who painted these images?

00:24:32.930 --> 00:24:36.309
What race of man

00:24:32.930 --> 00:24:36.309
was ever so glorious,

00:24:36.351 --> 00:24:39.396
that they filled

00:24:36.351 --> 00:24:39.396
our world with such,

00:24:39.437 --> 00:24:42.273
as you say,

00:24:39.437 --> 00:24:42.273
indescribable beauty?

00:24:44.984 --> 00:24:47.278
I have been told, sire,

00:24:47.320 --> 00:24:50.698
that you served at the court,

00:24:47.320 --> 00:24:50.698
of the emperor Charlemagne,

00:24:50.740 --> 00:24:53.534
which I have

00:24:50.740 --> 00:24:53.534
also visited.

00:24:53.576 --> 00:24:56.996
I cannot imagine,

00:24:53.576 --> 00:24:56.996
therefore, that you

00:24:53.576 --> 00:24:56.996
do not know what I know.

00:24:58.664 --> 00:25:01.251
That these images were

00:24:58.664 --> 00:25:01.251
painted by the Romans.

00:25:01.292 --> 00:25:03.336
They conquered these

00:25:01.292 --> 00:25:03.336
lands a long time ago.

00:25:03.378 --> 00:25:05.213
They conquered

00:25:03.378 --> 00:25:05.213
the whole world.

00:25:07.090 --> 00:25:08.591
But they were pagans.

00:25:09.592 --> 00:25:11.510
They worshipped false gods.

00:25:14.889 --> 00:25:19.394
Never speak of

00:25:14.889 --> 00:25:19.394
our conversation

00:25:14.889 --> 00:25:19.394
to any other man here.

00:25:19.436 --> 00:25:22.063
Nobody else would

00:25:19.436 --> 00:25:22.063
understand it.

00:25:22.105 --> 00:25:23.647
They would fear it.

00:25:23.689 --> 00:25:26.692
(LAUGHING)

00:25:23.689 --> 00:25:26.692
They accept

00:25:23.689 --> 00:25:26.692
an interpretation,

00:25:26.734 --> 00:25:30.238
that a race of giants

00:25:26.734 --> 00:25:30.238
once lived here.

00:25:30.280 --> 00:25:33.283
(LAUGHING)

00:25:30.280 --> 00:25:33.283
And that we have

00:25:30.280 --> 00:25:33.283
nothing to do with them.

00:25:33.866 --> 00:25:35.118
(CHUCKLES)

00:25:36.160 --> 00:25:38.204
The fact is, Athelstan,

00:25:40.206 --> 00:25:44.043
we have lost more

00:25:40.206 --> 00:25:44.043
knowledge than we

00:25:40.206 --> 00:25:44.043
ever had!

00:25:46.003 --> 00:25:50.007
These Romans knew things

00:25:46.003 --> 00:25:50.007
that we will never know!

00:25:50.049 --> 00:25:53.928
Their pagan gods allowed

00:25:50.049 --> 00:25:53.928
them to rule the world.

00:25:57.140 --> 00:25:59.892
And what is the

00:25:57.140 --> 00:25:59.892
lesson that we can

00:25:57.140 --> 00:25:59.892
learn from that?

00:26:02.812 --> 00:26:04.563
(MUSIC PLAYING)

00:26:12.238 --> 00:26:13.239
(MUSIC STOPS)

00:26:24.375 --> 00:26:26.169
What do you want,

00:26:24.375 --> 00:26:26.169
master?

00:26:27.962 --> 00:26:30.507
Forgive me.

00:26:27.962 --> 00:26:30.507
I just came to listen.

00:26:31.508 --> 00:26:33.676
You won't like

00:26:31.508 --> 00:26:33.676
our music.

00:26:33.717 --> 00:26:34.677
It's rough.

00:26:37.888 --> 00:26:39.182
I would still like

00:26:37.888 --> 00:26:39.182
to stay.

00:26:40.350 --> 00:26:41.809
That is,

00:26:40.350 --> 00:26:41.809
if you allow it.

00:26:44.645 --> 00:26:45.604
(MUSIC PLAYING)

00:28:31.294 --> 00:28:32.711
(TREMBLING BREATHING)

00:28:33.337 --> 00:28:34.838
AETHELWULF: Monk.

00:28:34.880 --> 00:28:37.133
(GASPS)

00:28:34.880 --> 00:28:37.133
My father desires

00:28:34.880 --> 00:28:37.133
to see you.

00:28:52.565 --> 00:28:54.733
Father's waiting for you

00:28:52.565 --> 00:28:54.733
behind this door.

00:29:12.209 --> 00:29:13.544
Come and see.

00:29:17.006 --> 00:29:18.215
Look around.

00:29:24.221 --> 00:29:27.517
You thought those

00:29:24.221 --> 00:29:27.517
paintings were all

00:29:24.221 --> 00:29:27.517
that there was.

00:29:36.233 --> 00:29:40.154
But of all Roman

00:29:36.233 --> 00:29:40.154
things, these are

00:29:36.233 --> 00:29:40.154
the most precious.

00:29:43.032 --> 00:29:45.660
Tales of the Caesars.

00:29:45.702 --> 00:29:48.621
The fall and ruin

00:29:45.702 --> 00:29:48.621
of Roman Britain.

00:29:48.663 --> 00:29:51.541
Tales of emperors

00:29:48.663 --> 00:29:51.541
and empires...

00:29:52.916 --> 00:29:55.294
It's the stuff of

00:29:52.916 --> 00:29:55.294
dreams, Athelstan.

00:29:56.795 --> 00:29:59.798
It's the very

00:29:56.795 --> 00:29:59.798
fabric of dreams.

00:30:03.761 --> 00:30:06.138
You can read them,

00:30:03.761 --> 00:30:06.138
of course.

00:30:18.526 --> 00:30:21.529
Yes. Yes, I can

00:30:18.526 --> 00:30:21.529
read them.

00:30:21.571 --> 00:30:23.155
Good.

00:30:23.197 --> 00:30:25.199
That is why

00:30:23.197 --> 00:30:25.199
I've chosen you.

00:30:32.206 --> 00:30:33.791
What do you mean?

00:30:33.832 --> 00:30:36.753
Well, I've chosen you

00:30:33.832 --> 00:30:36.753
to be the guardian, of

00:30:33.832 --> 00:30:36.753
these books

00:30:36.794 --> 00:30:38.128
and their secrets.

00:30:38.170 --> 00:30:40.715
I want you to copy them.

00:30:40.757 --> 00:30:43.467
You speak Latin,

00:30:40.757 --> 00:30:43.467
not many do.

00:30:43.509 --> 00:30:46.679
Your job will be to

00:30:43.509 --> 00:30:46.679
preserve these works

00:30:46.721 --> 00:30:47.971
and these...

00:30:49.181 --> 00:30:50.433
Fragments,

00:30:51.934 --> 00:30:53.852
for all eternity.

00:30:57.732 --> 00:31:01.736
But if you ever tell

00:30:57.732 --> 00:31:01.736
anyone about them,

00:31:01.778 --> 00:31:04.363
I will let them

00:31:01.778 --> 00:31:04.363
crucify you.

00:31:35.060 --> 00:31:37.896
I hope you were telling

00:31:35.060 --> 00:31:37.896
me the truth, Rollo.

00:31:39.523 --> 00:31:41.233
Why don't you ask her?

00:31:50.827 --> 00:31:52.202
(INDISTINCT CONVERSATIONS)

00:32:04.340 --> 00:32:05.842
Jarl Borg.

00:32:17.186 --> 00:32:18.521
Please.

00:32:22.316 --> 00:32:24.735
Earl Ragnar Lothbrok,

00:32:27.488 --> 00:32:29.406
can I say,

00:32:27.488 --> 00:32:29.406
in all honesty,

00:32:32.368 --> 00:32:36.497
you're a greater

00:32:32.368 --> 00:32:36.497
man than I am.

00:32:36.539 --> 00:32:39.583
I know, I don't deserve

00:32:36.539 --> 00:32:39.583
the chance, you have given me,

00:32:36.539 --> 00:32:39.583
to raid and work with you,

00:32:39.625 --> 00:32:41.460
but I swear on my ring,

00:32:43.379 --> 00:32:46.674
from henceforth,

00:32:43.379 --> 00:32:46.674
you've no reason

00:32:43.379 --> 00:32:46.674
to doubt my loyalty,

00:32:46.716 --> 00:32:48.759
or my commitment

00:32:46.716 --> 00:32:48.759
to our common cause.

00:32:50.720 --> 00:32:51.970
If we are being honest,

00:32:54.014 --> 00:32:56.225
I can tell you that

00:32:54.014 --> 00:32:56.225
it was King Horik,

00:32:56.266 --> 00:32:58.853
who argued for

00:32:56.266 --> 00:32:58.853
a renewal of our

00:32:56.266 --> 00:32:58.853
alliance.

00:33:00.813 --> 00:33:02.565
As you can imagine,

00:33:04.316 --> 00:33:06.985
I was not, at first,

00:33:04.316 --> 00:33:06.985
enthusiastic.

00:33:11.281 --> 00:33:12.533
But then...

00:33:14.243 --> 00:33:17.872
Then I realized

00:33:14.243 --> 00:33:17.872
what could be

00:33:14.243 --> 00:33:17.872
gained by inviting you.

00:33:20.207 --> 00:33:24.294
We have much to gain

00:33:20.207 --> 00:33:24.294
if we work together,

00:33:24.336 --> 00:33:26.547
and a lot to

00:33:24.336 --> 00:33:26.547
lose if we don't.

00:33:28.841 --> 00:33:30.968
Even I can see that now.

00:33:31.635 --> 00:33:33.011
(CHUCKLES)

00:33:35.514 --> 00:33:36.974
(LAUGHING)

00:33:39.518 --> 00:33:40.811
Torstein.

00:33:42.479 --> 00:33:44.147
Yes, My Lord.

00:33:44.189 --> 00:33:47.902
Put Jarl Borg's men

00:33:44.189 --> 00:33:47.902
in the barn which

00:33:44.189 --> 00:33:47.902
the servants use.

00:33:47.944 --> 00:33:50.112
And treat them

00:33:47.944 --> 00:33:50.112
with respect.

00:33:50.153 --> 00:33:52.489
Of course, My Lord.

00:33:55.618 --> 00:33:57.244
Thank you.

00:34:03.918 --> 00:34:05.628
HORIK: Siggy.

00:34:05.669 --> 00:34:10.090
I never once for a moment

00:34:05.669 --> 00:34:10.090
imagined, Ragnar

00:34:05.669 --> 00:34:10.090
would take my advice,

00:34:10.132 --> 00:34:13.844
and invite Jarl Borg,

00:34:10.132 --> 00:34:13.844
to rejoin our alliance.

00:34:13.886 --> 00:34:16.889
As I told you,

00:34:13.886 --> 00:34:16.889
Ragnar is different.

00:34:16.931 --> 00:34:19.099
Whatever you think

00:34:16.931 --> 00:34:19.099
he will do,

00:34:19.141 --> 00:34:22.227
he will always

00:34:19.141 --> 00:34:22.227
do the opposite.

00:34:22.269 --> 00:34:24.939
And I wanted to thank you

00:34:24.981 --> 00:34:27.441
for what you did

00:34:24.981 --> 00:34:27.441
for my son.

00:34:27.483 --> 00:34:29.192
You made him a man.

00:34:29.234 --> 00:34:32.070
Do not ask me to do

00:34:29.234 --> 00:34:32.070
it for your other sons.

00:34:33.322 --> 00:34:34.865
I am not a whore.

00:34:34.907 --> 00:34:37.785
No. Just for me.

00:34:52.716 --> 00:34:54.677
Can you keep a secret?

00:34:54.718 --> 00:34:56.804
(CHUCKLING) No.

00:35:04.436 --> 00:35:05.855
(MUSIC PLAYING)

00:35:12.486 --> 00:35:13.696
(SIGHING)

00:35:16.114 --> 00:35:18.158
What's the matter

00:35:16.114 --> 00:35:18.158
with you, my love?

00:35:21.119 --> 00:35:23.330
You don't talk,

00:35:21.119 --> 00:35:23.330
you don't smile.

00:35:49.065 --> 00:35:51.400
My love, you must

00:35:49.065 --> 00:35:51.400
do better than this.

00:35:55.153 --> 00:35:57.155
You know something?

00:35:59.366 --> 00:36:03.161
My wife has

00:35:59.366 --> 00:36:03.161
got the most

00:35:59.366 --> 00:36:03.161
beautiful breasts.

00:36:03.871 --> 00:36:05.873
I keep telling her,

00:36:07.374 --> 00:36:10.002
but she doesn't

00:36:07.374 --> 00:36:10.002
believe me.

00:36:10.044 --> 00:36:14.172
She has the most

00:36:10.044 --> 00:36:14.172
beautiful breasts

00:36:10.044 --> 00:36:14.172
in the world.

00:36:15.215 --> 00:36:16.299
(INDISTINCT MURMURING)

00:36:17.718 --> 00:36:19.803
They're like

00:36:17.718 --> 00:36:19.803
Freya's breasts.

00:36:20.888 --> 00:36:23.015
The breasts of a goddess.

00:36:25.559 --> 00:36:27.269
Let me show you.

00:36:30.147 --> 00:36:31.231
(ALL GASP)

00:36:31.273 --> 00:36:32.232
(SCREAMING)

00:36:46.997 --> 00:36:48.206
(ALL GASP)

00:36:51.543 --> 00:36:52.795
(HUSHED CHATTERING)

00:37:04.765 --> 00:37:07.143
ASLAUG: The giant king's

00:37:04.765 --> 00:37:07.143
servants,

00:37:07.184 --> 00:37:09.478
carried a trencher

00:37:07.184 --> 00:37:09.478
into the hall,

00:37:09.519 --> 00:37:12.648
and set it down

00:37:09.519 --> 00:37:12.648
before the throne.

00:37:12.689 --> 00:37:16.318
They heaped it with

00:37:12.689 --> 00:37:16.318
hunks of chopped meat,

00:37:16.359 --> 00:37:19.655
and it reminded Thor,

00:37:16.359 --> 00:37:19.655
that rather too

00:37:16.359 --> 00:37:19.655
long had gone, by

00:37:19.696 --> 00:37:21.031
since they had last eaten.

00:37:22.365 --> 00:37:24.827
Thor was so hungry!

00:37:24.868 --> 00:37:29.456
A chair was provided

00:37:24.868 --> 00:37:29.456
for Loki, at one end

00:37:24.868 --> 00:37:29.456
of the trencher,

00:37:29.498 --> 00:37:31.667
and for Logi at the other.

00:37:37.756 --> 00:37:39.257
(EAGLE CALLING)

00:37:56.108 --> 00:37:58.986
ASLAUG: <i> At the word from</i>

00:37:56.108 --> 00:37:58.986
<i>the giant king,</i>

00:37:59.028 --> 00:38:01.279
<i>they both began to eat.</i>

00:38:02.739 --> 00:38:06.576
They gobbled and

00:38:02.739 --> 00:38:06.576
consumed and...

00:38:06.618 --> 00:38:07.744
(BOTH GIGGLING)

00:38:09.287 --> 00:38:12.415
Each of them ate as

00:38:09.287 --> 00:38:12.415
fast as they could,

00:38:12.457 --> 00:38:14.459
edging their chair forward,

00:38:14.501 --> 00:38:17.587
and they met at

00:38:14.501 --> 00:38:17.587
the middle of the trencher.

00:38:19.173 --> 00:38:22.509
Loki had eaten

00:38:19.173 --> 00:38:22.509
every scrap of meat,

00:38:22.551 --> 00:38:24.887
and left nothing

00:38:22.551 --> 00:38:24.887
but the bones.

00:38:36.899 --> 00:38:38.275
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

00:38:42.946 --> 00:38:44.406
Where are you going?

00:38:57.335 --> 00:39:01.548
But Logi had not

00:38:57.335 --> 00:39:01.548
only eaten the meat,

00:39:01.590 --> 00:39:05.302
he had eaten the bones

00:39:01.590 --> 00:39:05.302
and the trencher as well.

00:39:06.053 --> 00:39:07.721
I think Logi won.

00:39:09.765 --> 00:39:10.599
(GRUNTING)

00:39:27.157 --> 00:39:28.658
(WATER DRIPPING)

00:39:34.623 --> 00:39:35.999
(FOOTSTEPS)

00:39:39.044 --> 00:39:40.378
Who is it?

00:39:44.967 --> 00:39:47.177
SEER: Yes, I can see,

00:39:47.219 --> 00:39:49.429
and I see an eagle.

00:39:51.932 --> 00:39:55.393
I see that an eagle

00:39:51.932 --> 00:39:55.393
hovers over you.

00:39:57.354 --> 00:40:00.023
But I also see

00:40:00.065 --> 00:40:03.235
that you yourself

00:40:00.065 --> 00:40:03.235
are the eagle.

00:40:22.879 --> 00:40:26.675
ASLAUG: <i> "I would say,"</i>

00:40:22.879 --> 00:40:26.675
<i>proclaimed the giant king,</i>

00:40:28.218 --> 00:40:31.429
<i>"that Loki is the loser."</i>

00:40:32.889 --> 00:40:36.268
(WHISPERING) Hush, Ubbe.

00:40:32.889 --> 00:40:36.268
Hvitserk is nearly asleep.

00:40:36.310 --> 00:40:37.853
Now you go to sleep.

00:40:37.894 --> 00:40:39.146
I don't want to.

00:40:40.272 --> 00:40:41.357
Why not?

00:40:42.149 --> 00:40:43.942
Because whenever you dream,

00:40:43.984 --> 00:40:47.112
you never know what

00:40:43.984 --> 00:40:47.112
is going to happen.

00:41:06.006 --> 00:41:07.049
(MEN GROANING)

00:41:07.090 --> 00:41:08.175
MAN: What's happening?

00:41:08.217 --> 00:41:09.426
What?

00:41:10.177 --> 00:41:12.346
All you folk in the barn.

00:41:12.388 --> 00:41:14.973
If you want to live,

00:41:12.388 --> 00:41:14.973
stay silent.

00:41:15.932 --> 00:41:18.018
Nothing will happen to you.

00:41:28.653 --> 00:41:29.946
ALL: No!

00:41:28.653 --> 00:41:29.946
No! Fire!

00:41:32.991 --> 00:41:34.492
(MEN SHOUTING)

00:41:35.827 --> 00:41:37.704
WOMAN: Let us out!

00:41:35.827 --> 00:41:37.704
WOMAN 2: Let us out!

00:41:45.003 --> 00:41:46.755
ROLLO: Where have you been?

00:41:46.796 --> 00:41:50.592
Here and there.

00:41:46.796 --> 00:41:50.592
Up and down.

00:41:50.633 --> 00:41:53.803
Where is Bjorn?

00:41:50.633 --> 00:41:53.803
He is supposed

00:41:50.633 --> 00:41:53.803
to be with you.

00:41:55.431 --> 00:41:57.474
I don't know, Rollo.

00:41:59.559 --> 00:42:00.769
Let's go.

00:42:07.776 --> 00:42:09.527
It is fine, come.

00:42:20.663 --> 00:42:22.249
You can sleep here.

00:42:26.586 --> 00:42:28.546
No, I can't.

00:42:29.589 --> 00:42:31.549
Of course you can.

00:42:29.589 --> 00:42:31.549
Why not?

00:42:33.676 --> 00:42:35.720
This is your place.

00:42:35.762 --> 00:42:37.055
I cannot sleep here.

00:42:38.098 --> 00:42:39.557
Well, don't you want to?

00:42:40.517 --> 00:42:43.561
What does it matter

00:42:40.517 --> 00:42:43.561
what I want to do?

00:42:45.772 --> 00:42:48.817
Well, what if

00:42:45.772 --> 00:42:48.817
I ordered you

00:42:45.772 --> 00:42:48.817
to stay here?

00:42:51.194 --> 00:42:53.571
Then I would have to

00:42:55.198 --> 00:42:56.574
heed your command.

00:43:00.162 --> 00:43:01.788
I don't want to order you.

00:43:04.124 --> 00:43:06.209
I want you to

00:43:04.124 --> 00:43:06.209
choose to stay here.

00:43:16.303 --> 00:43:18.138
Is this what

00:43:16.303 --> 00:43:18.138
you want?

00:43:19.097 --> 00:43:20.182
Master?

00:43:30.733 --> 00:43:32.361
Good evening, Jarl Borg.

00:43:35.113 --> 00:43:36.114
(GRUNTING)

00:43:47.334 --> 00:43:49.002
(SIGHING)

00:43:49.044 --> 00:43:50.504
I told you...

00:43:51.629 --> 00:43:54.049
I always look for revenge.

00:43:56.009 --> 00:43:57.427
(GROANING)

00:44:03.058 --> 00:44:04.226
(GRUNTING)

00:44:08.271 --> 00:44:09.398
No!

00:44:08.271 --> 00:44:09.398
(GASPS)

00:44:09.439 --> 00:44:11.066
(MUFFLED GRUNT)

00:44:11.107 --> 00:44:12.568
Not necessary.

00:44:17.030 --> 00:44:17.822
(GRUNTING)

00:44:38.051 --> 00:44:39.094
(ROARING)

00:44:43.723 --> 00:44:45.683
What is all the commotion?

00:44:49.104 --> 00:44:50.564
LOTHBROK: I am sorry,

00:44:52.023 --> 00:44:54.484
that the ambiance

00:44:52.023 --> 00:44:54.484
of Kattegat,

00:44:55.277 --> 00:44:56.694
has awoken you.

00:44:58.071 --> 00:44:59.448
What is the cause of this?

00:45:00.156 --> 00:45:00.990
MAN: In here!

00:45:14.879 --> 00:45:17.382
HORIK: Is he dead?

00:45:14.879 --> 00:45:17.382
FLOKI: No, no, no.

00:45:18.216 --> 00:45:19.759
FLOKI: He's not dead.

00:45:20.176 --> 00:45:21.303
Yet.

00:45:22.095 --> 00:45:22.971
(GRUNTING)

00:45:30.395 --> 00:45:32.147
Why have you done this?

00:45:32.188 --> 00:45:34.608
Did you really think,

00:45:32.188 --> 00:45:34.608
that I could ever

00:45:32.188 --> 00:45:34.608
forgive this man,

00:45:35.733 --> 00:45:37.860
for threatening

00:45:35.733 --> 00:45:37.860
to kill my family?

00:45:39.446 --> 00:45:40.738
So, what will you do now?

00:45:52.917 --> 00:45:55.878
Since you consort

00:45:52.917 --> 00:45:55.878
with eagles,

00:45:55.920 --> 00:45:58.840
I will draw a blood eagle

00:45:55.920 --> 00:45:58.840
on your back.

00:46:02.010 --> 00:46:02.802
No.

00:46:03.679 --> 00:46:05.305
And your ribcage

00:46:06.222 --> 00:46:07.765
will spring apart.

00:46:16.525 --> 00:46:17.775
No.

00:46:20.195 --> 00:46:21.655
Yes.

00:46:31.206 --> 00:46:32.790
Like wings.